# Normalise to LF in the repo. Authored on Windows, but CI, Docker, and the
# Hugging Face Space all run Linux -- a CRLF shell script there fails with an
# opaque "bad interpreter" error, so pin the executable formats explicitly.
* text=auto eol=lf

*.py   text eol=lf
*.toml text eol=lf
*.yml  text eol=lf
*.yaml text eol=lf
*.md   text eol=lf
*.sh   text eol=lf
*.txt  text eol=lf
Dockerfile text eol=lf

# Windows-only helper scripts keep CRLF.
*.bat  text eol=crlf
*.ps1  text eol=crlf

# Never munge binaries or notebook payloads.
# `*.bin` is not decorative: `web/public/data/embeddings.bin` is tracked, and
# `text=auto` above would otherwise decide its type by looking for a NUL byte
# in the first 8 KB. Float32 vectors nearly always contain one, so it would
# nearly always guess right -- and the failure mode of guessing wrong is CRLF
# translation silently rewriting bytes inside the embeddings on a Windows
# checkout. "Nearly always" is not a serialisation guarantee.
*.bin  binary
*.png  binary
*.jpg  binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif  binary
*.npy  binary
*.onnx binary
*.faiss binary
*.parquet binary

# Notebooks: diff as text, but do not let Git rewrite embedded outputs.
*.ipynb text eol=lf
